# Wave W17-Q (Route 124): trench rock — trench-rim rock standing in the lane’s water: a dark blue-grey rim block, massive and sheer where the trench drops away beside it, pale only at its foam collar, the sea baked in around it (design: the dark dive trench showing through the surface mid-route — the rim the divers go down beside). Route 124’s own rock — the darkest rock in Maris: split from Route 122’s red-banded shoulder by colour and mood (blue-grey dark vs rust bands) and from Route 106’s near-black crag by form (a sheer rim block, not a crag cluster).
